DL is a sub domain of AI and ML that is inspired by the structure of a human brain.
Logical structures called neural network.
The fundamental unit of each neural network is called "perceptron".

TYPES OF NEURAL NETWORKS-
1. MULTI LAYERED PERCEPTRON- used in supervised problems
2. ANN -> ARTIFICIAL NEURAL NETWORK 
3. CNN -> CONVOLUTIONAL NEURAL NETWORK -> works with image data.
4. RNN -> RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORK -> works with speech and textual data. (lstm)
5. GAN -> GENERATIVE ADVERSARIAL NETWORK -> can generate texts, images etc.
6. Auto-encoders -> compression withour loosing quality


WHY DO WE NEED DL?
1. In applications like chemist drugs, automated cars etc.
2. High performance. 

TECHNICAL DEFINITION-
Representation learning - automatically extracting the features ( unlike in ml we have to do feature engineering to provide features to the model).
So in DL there is no need for feature extraction separately.
Neural network has layered structure. Initial layers extract the primitive features and the deep layers extract the complex features.

Less data -> ML performs better
more data -> DL performs well
training time in DL is more than ML.
less prediction time in DL.
explanability and interpretability in ML is high.
DL need gpu based hardware which is expensive.

